// MileLog — Supabase credentials
//
// SETUP (once):
//   1. cp Secrets.xcconfig.example Secrets.xcconfig
//   2. Fill in the two values below from your Supabase project's
//      Settings → API page.
//   3. In Xcode: select the MileLog PROJECT (not the target) → Info →
//      Configurations → expand Debug and Release → set both to Secrets.
//
// Secrets.xcconfig is gitignored. This .example file is not — keep real
// values out of it.
//
// Why a config file rather than typing into Info.plist: the plist is
// committed, so credentials pasted there end up in git history. Info.plist
// references these as $(SUPABASE_URL) / $(SUPABASE_ANON_KEY) and the build
// substitutes them.

SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your_publishable_or_anon_key_here

// Note the $() in the URL above — that is not a typo. xcconfig treats a
// double slash as a comment, so $() breaks the sequence without appearing
// in the resulting value. Keep it when you paste your real URL.
